WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:05.180
Hercules: The Legendary Journeys was silly,
campy, and a lot of fun to watch.

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:09.460
The '90s TV phenomenon earned a dedicated
worldwide fanbase—and generated the successful

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:12.470
spinoffs Young Hercules and Xena: Warrior
Princess.

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:16.340
Let's take a look back at the pantheon of
stars from the Hercules universe, and find

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:17.660
out where they are today.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.120
Kevin Sorbo

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:24.600
From 1995 to 1999, Kevin Sorbo starred as
the title character of Hercules: The Legendary

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:25.200
Journeys.

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:29.600
In the show, Hercules adventured through ancient
Europe, confronting evil beings and other

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:30.840
challenges along the way.

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:34.440
Despite facing challenges with his personal
health—like the three strokes he suffered

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:38.579
because of an aneurysm in his shoulder—Sorbo
has continued acting, starring in projects

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:42.560
like the sci-fi drama series Andromeda from
2000 to 2005.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:47.180
More recently, Sorbo had a recurring role
in the CW series Supergirl, and he's lined

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:50.700
up nearly a dozen films for release in 2017
and 2018.

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:52.100
Michael Hurst

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:56.640
New Zealand native Michael Hurst co-starred
in The Legendary Journeys as Iolaus, friend

00:00:56.649 --> 00:00:58.300
and sidekick to Hercules.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:02.920
Like Sorbo, Hurst reprised his role in a few
episodes of the Hercules spinoff show, Xena:

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:03.920
Warrior Princess.

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:07.080
He has continued acting since Hercules, and
he's also turned his attention to writing

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:07.800
and directing.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:12.320
He's recently directed episodes of Ash vs.
Evil Dead and the New Zealand show Westside.

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:13.620
Lucy Lawless

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:18.590
What started out as a guest role on Hercules:
The Legendary Journeys turned into a career-making

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:23.400
move for Lucy Lawless when she was given her
own spin-off series, Xena: Warrior Princess.

00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:27.060
Lawless has maintained a successful acting
career since then, appearing in dozens of

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:28.040
films and shows.

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:32.520
Notably, she guest-starred in 16 episodes
of Battlestar Galactica and in the Starz series

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:33.400
Spartacus.

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:38.020
Lawless also had a recurring role on Parks
and Recreation, and a major part on Ash vs

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:38.520
Evil Dead.

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:40.180
Robert Trebor

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:44.160
When Hercules wasn't partnered with Iolaus
for an adventure, he frequently traveled with

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:47.240
the crafty salesman Salmoneus, played by Robert
Trebor.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:51.260
Trebor has continued to appear in television
shows and on the big screen, landing a list

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:54.400
of parts that includes guest roles in Boomtown
and The Devil's Rejects.

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:59.420
Most recently, Trebor played "The Producer"
in the 2016 Coen brothers comedy Hail, Caesar!

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:00.920
Jeffrey Thomas

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:05.400
For 16 episodes of Hercules, Jeffrey Thomas
played the legendary ruler King Jason.

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:09.900
Thomas later appeared as Titus in the Starz
series Spartacus and the dwarf king Thror

00:02:09.909 --> 00:02:11.560
in The Hobbit: An Unexpected Journey.

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:14.340
In 2015, he starred in the horror film The
Dead Room.

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:19.000
More recently, Thomas appeared in The Light
Between Oceans alongside Alicia Vikander and

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:19.980
Michael Fassbender.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:21.280
Kevin Tod Smith

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:25.640
New Zealand actor Kevin Tod Smith landed a
major recurring role on Hercules and the Xena

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:27.680
spinoff as Ares, the God of War.

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:31.840
Between the two shows, he starred in over
50 episodes, often filming for both productions

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:32.620
at the same time.

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:36.640
Smith seemed to have a promising career ahead
of him, and was cast to appear in the Bruce

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:40.540
Willis war drama Tears of the Sun, but he
passed away before he could film the part.

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:44.780
Smith accidentally fell from a prop tower
and suffered major injuries which led to his

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:47.140
death on February 15th, 2002.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:48.300
Bruce Campbell

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:52.800
Although he's much better known for his role
as Ash in the Evil Dead franchise, Bruce Campbell

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:57.599
starred in The Legendary Journeys and Xena:
Warrior Princess as Autolycus—the self-proclaimed

00:02:57.599 --> 00:03:01.629
"King of Thieves" who occasionally assists
Hercules and Xena on their adventures.

00:03:01.629 --> 00:03:03.999
Campbell was also an executive producer for
Hercules.

00:03:03.999 --> 00:03:07.719
Campbell has appeared in dozens of films and
television shows in the years since.

00:03:07.719 --> 00:03:11.700
Most recently, he returned to his roots by
starring in the Starz comedy/action series

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:13.160
Ash vs Evil Dead.

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:14.980
Alexandra Tydings

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:20.520
For 10 episodes of Hercules and 11 episodes
of Xena, Alexandra Tydings played Aphrodite,

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:23.040
the Greek goddess of love and half-sister
of Hercules.

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:28.080
Despite the "dumb blonde" stereotype she portrayed
as Aphrodite, Tydings is one smart cookie.

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:32.460
She largely retired from acting after Xena
and turned her attention to writing and directing.

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:33.880
Gina Torres

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:38.540
While she's better known these days for her
role as Zoe in Firefly, many fans will remember

00:03:38.549 --> 00:03:41.279
Gina Torres as the pirate Nebula from Hercules.

00:03:41.279 --> 00:03:46.370
Torres has had a strong Hollywood career since
Hercules, landing major roles in 24, Cleopatra

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:48.090
2525, and Alias.

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:52.810
More recently, she appeared in the ABC series
The Catch and provided the voice of Ikora

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:54.620
Rey in the video game Destiny 2.

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:55.900
Joel Tobeck

00:03:56.420 --> 00:04:00.599
While he primarily played the Greek god Strife
in The Legendary Journeys, Joel Tobeck also

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:03.640
appeared as Strife's cousin Deimos in both
Hercules and Xena.

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:07.939
In addition to a significant role in Sons
of Anarchy, Tobeck later reunited with several

00:04:07.939 --> 00:04:12.109
of his castmates for other projects, including
Bruce Campbell and Lucy Lawless in Ash vs

00:04:12.109 --> 00:04:12.660
Evil Dead.

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:13.760
Thanks for watching!

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:16.540
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:16.549 --> 00:04:18.619
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

